Lung ultrasound &ndash; interpretation

Pneumothorax

&CenterDot; 
Seen in non-dependent areas 

&CenterDot; 
Lung point present (gold standard)

&CenterDot; 
Clearer A lines

&CenterDot; 
No B lines

&CenterDot; 
No sliding

&CenterDot; 
No sea shore sign

Effusion

&CenterDot; 
Seen in dependent areas, easiest with patient upright 

&CenterDot; 
Hypoechoic collection

&CenterDot; 
Collapsed lung swimming about

Oedema

&CenterDot; 
More than three B lines. Like disco lights.

Pneumonia

&CenterDot; 
Hepatisation (i.e. looks solid)

&CenterDot; 
Air bronchograms (i.e. white branches)

&CenterDot; 
If early pneumonia: localised patch of B lines, subpleural
densities

